{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:92368",
  "title": "Important: curl security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-30 12:01:09"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-31 00:13:19"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The curl packages provide the libcurl library and the curl utility for downloading files from servers using various protocols, including HTTP, FTP, and LDAP.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* libcurl: libcurl: Security feature bypass due to improper mTLS connection reuse (CVE-2026-8932)\n\n* curl: libcurl: Unauthorized connection reuse due to a logical error (CVE-2026-8458)\n\n* curl: curl: Cookie injection via malicious HTTP server using super cookies (CVE-2026-8924)\n\n* curl: curl: Information disclosure via incorrect Digest authentication header reuse (CVE-2026-11856)\n\n* curl: Information disclosure due to uncleared proxy authentication state (CVE-2026-8927)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Backport upstream curl PR #6852 (\"h2: allow 100 streams by default\") to Rocky Linux 8 libcurl (JIRA:Rocky Linux-232829)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
